  "highest_admissible_claim": "JANUS has recovered the exact historical LinearAInscriptions.js input identified by the Briakos thesis receipt and admitted a non-executing JavaScript-Map-compatible parser for that source. A clean replay on those exact bytes does not reproduce the published Briakos metric vector under the frozen JANUS method manifest; multiple predeclared or externally fixed 419-scope explanations were tested and rejected without post-hoc subset search, so the public corpus-selection/method scope remains unresolved rather than refuted. The related historical annotations.js repository candidate is strongly supported by two independent path-history transports and by an exact match between the thesis numeric size 2201442 and the decoded Unicode code-point count, while its raw UTF-8 size is 2239932; JANUS does not infer the author's measurement implementation or claim a byte-count-exact receipt. The annotation identity layer does not reconstruct the 419-document corpus. External logos D5 and corrected D6 source-layer defects were replayed as prior art, and a backward-compatible v1.1 IR hardening profile is admitted to represent cross-surface continuations and unresolved sign-identity conflicts without destructive merging or semantic promotion. None of these R3C results supply the independent alternate-editorial source bytes required by R3B, establish a new linguistic anchor, or constitute a decipherment. Additionally, a real-source coverage audit established that the four externally seeded D5 splits are mechanically present in the current mwenge source but the flat source exposes only newline/line-break witnesses and does not resolve whether each boundary is a physical surface transition or a ruled-line transition. An additive v1.2.1 hardening profile is admitted, preserving v1.1 and the base IR format while representing SOURCE_CONTINUATION_ACROSS_BOUNDARY with SURFACE, LINE, or UNRESOLVED_SURFACE_OR_LINE classes and fail-closed claim-view policies. A seven-document minimal source-span projection has passed cumulative base/v1.1/v1.2.1 validation and negative/positive scientific-view firewall canaries for all four D5 and three D6 cases. These are technical source-span projections, not full-document transcriptions; D5 boundary kind and linguistic wordhood remain unresolved, and D6 assigns no semantics to A319/*904. The R3C-3 corrective language-match lane is now methodologically frozen against Nepal and Perono Cacciafoco (2024): the five-language family is fixed, the primary unit is the complete raw exact consonant-cluster match universe before manual semantic filtering, two pre-frozen matched null families and max-stat familywise control are implemented, and the runner passes deterministic synthetic validation. Scientific execution remains blocked because no paper-exact study-input receipt or admitted upstream normalization contract is present. The public packaged application and README are methodological prior art, not substitutes for paper-exact input identity. Therefore no published language match has been reproduced by this gate and no language-family relationship, anchor, independent transcription replication, or decipherment is established.",
